  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Settings Pane",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Quiet Settings Pane\"**\n\nThe UI reads like a pane of Apple's System Settings: a pale ground, white inset groups with hairline separators, plain sentences, the platform font, and a single system-blue accent reserved for controls and the live line. Density is comfortable and list-driven; nothing is a card grid, and nothing glows for its own sake. Light and dark are both first-class, declared as one token set on `:root` and swapped under `prefers-color-scheme: dark`.\n\nExactly one physical object lives on the page: a cable (white like an Apple USB-C cable in light mode, graphite in dark) that runs from a boot on the status card's left edge to a port on the live row. Its plug carries a MagSafe-style status light. The status card's right side holds a WebGL dotted globe where each gateway request flies as a light from this computer to Anthropic. These two are the only illustrative elements; everything else is platform chrome.\n\nMotion is one physics. A critically damped spring is sampled into a CSS `linear()` easing at load and shared by CSS transitions and WAAPI animations; only a thrown plug is allowed to bounce. Exits are short and accelerate away.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Grouped inset lists on a tinted ground; hairline separators inset to the text column.",
      "One accent (system blue), semantic dots only (green, orange, red, gray).",
      "Platform font with size-specific negative tracking; mono only for keys, URLs, tokens.",
      "Translucency only where content passes beneath: toolbar, menu, toast.",
      "A single cable-and-plug object and a dotted globe as the only illustration.",
      "Spring motion, critically damped by default; reduced motion keeps every function."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Voice Rule",
        "body": "Blue appears only on controls, the live line and request traffic. Status is never blue; it is a green, orange, red or gray dot.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dot, Not Paint Rule",
        "body": "Semantic hues appear as small dots (7-8px), icons, the plug light or the switch, never as row or card backgrounds.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tracking Ladder Rule",
        "body": "Every size carries its own letter-spacing (from -0.024em at 28px to 0 at 12px and below). Don't reuse one tracking value across sizes.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Numbers Line Up Rule",
        "body": "Counts, times, durations and step numbers use tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Floats Only Rule",
        "body": "Groups never cast shadows. Only menus, toasts, sheets, the segmented thumb, the switch knob and the plug do.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Glass Where It Passes Rule",
        "body": "Blur only surfaces that content scrolls or sits beneath; never blur a static group for effect.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** build every new screen from inset groups on the grouped ground, with hairlines inset to the text column.",
      "**Do** keep blue for controls, the live line and request traffic; show status with a green, orange, red or gray dot plus a word.",
      "**Do** move things on the shared `--spring` / `--spring-ms` and leave on the exit easing; keep springs critically damped unless the user threw something.",
      "**Do** define every new colour as a `:root` token with a dark value, and check it under reduced transparency and increased contrast.",
      "**Do** use the platform font with its per-size tracking, and mono only for secrets, URLs and tokens."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add a second physical object or illustration beyond the cable, plug and globe.",
      "**Don't** use a dashboard card grid, glow or decorative glass; blur only the toolbar, menus, toasts and labels that float over content.",
      "**Don't** put shadows on groups at rest.",
      "**Don't** paint rows or groups in semantic colours.",
      "**Don't** let meaning depend on motion; every function must still work with reduced motion."
    ]
  }
}
